  "note": "iter31 loso-institution (measurer, ZERO code edits, no revert; stage = workspace pending_stage 'loso-institution'). Tree = PR #25 4-column base PLUS the ONE landed change: the pure C=1e-2 logistic log-odds in column 0 (iter30's 0.5/0.5 force-mix REMOVED) plus a fixed-config HistGradientBoostingClassifier (F=2000 from the SAME training-fold-only |t| ranking + age/sex, 60 iters, lr 0.1, 8 leaves, min_samples_leaf 15, l2 1.0, bins 64, no early stopping, seeded, unweighted) appended as ONE NEW FINAL fifth meta column in both OOF and held-out matrices (0.0 where unfittable). One fit per fold, model_selection = final fit; no best-epoch / no test-fold selection, so the 0.623->0.707 inflation does not apply. PRE-DECLARED DISCRIMINATORS: (1) institution AUC must not fall more than 0.005 below the iter30/PR base institution 0.7876 (i.e. FAIL below ~0.7826) even if ASD recall rises; genuine information needs institution AUC > ~0.805 (>1 institution fold SEM, SD ~0.094); (2) institution ASD recall vs base 0.7122, with control recall >= 0.73 and headroom above 0.7512 NOT credited as gain; (3) accept arithmetic needs delta >= +0.003 on one split with the other no worse than -0.005, and iter31 site already measured 0.7405 - 0.7448 = -0.43 pp, so a site-split accept is arithmetically unavailable and only an institution gain > +0.3 pp could accept. Report per-fold institution AUC/sens/spec, runtime vs the 120-min budget, whether result.json was written (none = runtime infeasibility, NOT a PASS), and any HGB / meta-weight diagnostics if they surface (measurement_notes EMPTY for 19 consecutive runs -> fired-vs-inert stays UNRESOLVED, not 'inert').",
